{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Adding or editing common media assets can cause the audit to block an otherwise permitted run."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Ordinary additions or edits to executable text scripts are incorrectly blocked as binary content."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid PNG with common metadata can cause the audit to block an otherwise permitted change."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Ordinary signature strings can misclassify readable text as binary, allowing a diff-hiding attribute rule to bypass its separate allowance check."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A small edit to a large text file can be blocked by an inspection output limit that allowances cannot clear."}]}